{number: 90}
{title: My Faith Looks Up to Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] My faith looks up to Thee,
[F] Thou Lamb of [G7] Calva-[C] ry,
Savior di-[G7] vine:
Now [C] hear me while I pray,
Take [F] all my [G7] guilt a-[C] way,
O [F] let me from this day
Be [G7] wholly [C] Thine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] May Thy rich grace impart
[F] Strength to my [G7] fainting [C] heart,
My zeal in-[G7] spire;
As [C] Thou hast died for me,
O [F] may my [G7] love to [C] Thee
Pure, [F] warm, and changeless be,
A [G7] living [C] fire!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] While life's dark maze I tread,
[F] And griefs a-[G7] round me [C] spread,
Be Thou my [G7] Guide;
Bid [C] darkness turn to day,
Wipe [F] sorrow's [G7] tears a-[C] way,
Nor [F] let me ever stray
From [G7] Thee a-[C] side.
{end_of_verse}
